# Git conventions

- Conventional Commits in English: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`,
  `test:`, `chore:`. Scope optional: `feat(core): ...`.
- One logical change per commit. Don't mix code and docs rewrites.
- `main` is always releasable; feature work on branches `feat/<slug>`.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, API keys, or recorded fixtures containing
  real user data.
- Commit messages describe WHY, not just WHAT, when the change is non-obvious.
